<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="f592f4a7-ecd8-4de0-949c-8c45dcf87b59" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerConceptualDocument
    xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5"
    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">

    <introduction>
      <para>The <legacyBold>tasks</legacyBold> element is used to configure a collection of tasks to be executed when schedules fire. By default, each task will be associated
               with all schedules, but can also be explicitly associated with one or more named schedules. 
                Supported elements are shown below.</para>
    </introduction>

    
                                    
    
<section>
	<content>
		<code language="xml">
            &lt;scheduler name=&quot;myscheduler&quot;&gt;
                &lt;tasks&gt;
                    &lt;task type="MyTask, MyTaskLibrary" /&gt;
                    &lt;CodeTask /&gt;
                    &lt;ApplicationTask /&gt;
                &lt;/tasks&gt;
            &lt;/scheduler&gt;
  		</code>
	</content>
</section>
                
           
<section>
	<title>Attributes and Elements</title>
 	<content>
 	
	<table>
		<title>Attributes</title>
   			<para>None</para>
	</table>
                
	<table>
		<title>
			Child Elements
		</title>
		
		<tableHeader>
			<row>
				<entry>
					Element
				</entry>
				<entry>
					Description
				</entry>
			</row>
		</tableHeader>
		
			<row>
				<entry>
					<legacyBold><link xlink:href="d790b6d8-8d98-4af9-9de0-70d22e267cba">task</link> </legacyBold>
				</entry>
				<entry>
					A custom or third-party task.
				</entry>
			</row>
			<row>
				<entry>
					<legacyBold><link xlink:href="9473b45f-5001-4440-a0ca-c4adddb69235">CodeTask</link> </legacyBold>
				</entry>
				<entry>
					Represents the built-in <codeEntityReference qualifyHint="false">T:DemiCode.Scheduling.Tasks.CodeTask</codeEntityReference> task.
				</entry>
			</row>
			<row>
				<entry>
					<legacyBold><link xlink:href="80913175-28b9-46b1-ae4c-455d8fc75d46">ApplicationTask</link> </legacyBold>
				</entry>
				<entry>
					Represents the built-in <codeEntityReference qualifyHint="false">T:DemiCode.Scheduling.Tasks.ApplicationTask</codeEntityReference> task.
				</entry>
			</row>
		</table>
  </content>
</section>

            

    

